{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make repeatedly feeding another person\u2019s pet after being told to stop an offence",
        "additional_details": "The person received a clear and evidenced instruction not to feed the animal;\r\nThey knew, or ought to have known, that the owner\u2019s consent had been refused or withdrawn;\r\nThey continued feeding or attempting to feed the animal; and\r\nTheir conduct caused, or created a significant risk of, illness, injury, poisoning, dietary harm, behavioural disturbance, distress, disappearance, other danger to the animal, or death.\r\nPolice and authorised animal-welfare inspectors should be able to investigate complaints and take enforcement action.\r\nThe offence should not apply to accidental feeding, veterinary treatment, authorised care, emergency action reasonably taken to prevent immediate suffering, or assistance given to an animal genuinely believed to be lost, abandoned or in immediate danger.",
        "background": "Create a specific criminal offence where a person, without lawful authority or reasonable excuse, feeds or attempts to feed another person\u2019s pet on two or more separate occasions and the owner or lawful keeper has clearly instructed them to stop.\r\nThe offence should require proof that:",
